    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# HA - Scrapping and Logging Human Sent Replies\n\n## Purpose\nKeeps Interaction_Logs in sync with what human agents actually reply to escalated customers. Without this, every escalation row sits as `response = Pending` forever and downstream automations (SLA monitor, KB updater, AI Agent context) cannot tell a case has been resolved.\n\n## How it works\n- Polls the support Gmail Sent folder every minute for messages sent in the last day\n- Filters to keep only messages sent in the last 5 minutes that are NOT the system's automated 'Request Forwarded to Support Team' confirmation\n- Looks up the matching Interaction_Logs row by threadId; skips threads that already have a non-pending response\n- Strips quoted-reply text from the agent's reply body and writes it back into the existing pending row, updating response, timestampEnd, response time, word count, message count, and flagging humanAgentReply = True\n- If an SLA_Breach_Logs row exists for the same thread, removes it (the breach is now resolved)\n\n## Triggered by\nSchedule trigger  every minute.\n\n## Reads/writes\n- Reads Gmail Sent folder\n- Reads/updates Google Sheets `Customer_Support_Data`  `Interaction_Logs` (matches by threadId, updates the pending escalation row)\n- Reads and deletes rows from Google Sheets `Customer_Support_Data`  `SLA_Breach_Logs` when the matching breach is resolved",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 1040,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "sticky-overview-doc",
      "name": "Workflow Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1200,
        -256
      ]
    }
